LOCUS       pJL1-T7-TetO-PLA1      3223 bp    DNA     circular SYN 12-OCT-2026
DEFINITION  TetR-repressed, aTc-inducible phospholipase A1 (PLA1) construct.
            Sequence carried verbatim from the Google Doc "TetO-PLA in
            NB_CPRG" (named pJL1_T7-TetO-PLA1 there, 2026-10-12); the Doc
            states this cassette sits on the reverse strand, confirmed here
            by locating the promoter/operator/RBS/CDS on the reverse
            complement of the given sequence.
ACCESSION   pJL1-T7-TetO-PLA1
VERSION     pJL1-T7-TetO-PLA1
KEYWORDS    .
SOURCE      .
  ORGANISM  .
            .
COMMENT     Built 2026-10-12 from the source Doc's inline sequence. The
            T7/tetO/RBS/CDS cassette sits on the reverse strand of the given
            sequence, as the Doc's own construct table states; features
            below are annotated with complement() locations against the
            Doc's sequence as supplied. CDS translates to 320 aa
            (MSMSLSFTSAIAPAAIQPP...ANA), the same PLA1 protein as
            mk-mb-devnote2 and mk-mb-devnote-4's pOpen-TetO-PLA, here on a
            different (pJL1) backbone. The AmpR marker is not annotated,
            since the Doc gives no landmark for it.
FEATURES             Location/Qualifiers
     source          1..3223
                     /mol_type="other DNA"
     promoter        complement(1841..1860)
                     /label="T7 promoter"
     protein_bind    complement(1821..1839)
                     /label="tetO operator"
     RBS             complement(1762..1775)
                     /label="RBS"
     CDS             complement(799..1761)
                     /label="PLA1"
                     /codon_start=1
                     /note="320 aa phospholipase A1, per the source Doc's
                     construct table; on the reverse strand"
